# Copy to hooks/channel-ceiling.conf to turn on the channel-file insertion ceiling in
# git-hooks/pre-commit. One LIMIT line (optional, default 100) plus one repo-relative
# glob pattern per line — matched with a plain bash `case` glob against the staged path,
# so "NOTES.md" matches only a top-level file and "*/NOTES.md" matches one in any folder.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# No file at all means this check never runs — the safe default for a repo with no shared
# files several people or sessions append to. Turn it on for the files where a much bigger
# jump than usual usually means two sessions' entries landed in the same commit.
LIMIT=100
NOTES.md
CHANGELOG.md
*/NOTES.md
